**Recap of iteration 7 (item 07, the 24 open dataset classes)**

Two of the 24 open classes are now closed, with certificates verified by the independent checker:

- **BalancedTree_3_5** (364 vertices): the branch lemma down the complete ternary tree, written as a nested separator-branch certificate (121 branch nodes, 243 trivial leaves), proves pathwidth at least 5, equal to the stored layout. The checker verifies all 364 nodes with no C re-run. The value is classical (Ellis, Sudborough and Turner 1994); the certificate is what is new. The C program had spent 237 core-hours on this class.
- **NY_13** (PACE 2017 bonus, 283 vertices, recorded width 10, floor 9): family M's search found an 85-vertex contraction minor whose pathwidth the C program proves to be 10 by refuting 9 in 67,455 nodes and 0.07 s. It passes the replay, the C re-proof and the rule-free check (1.17 M refuted prefixes, 1.9 s). This is the one class where the search beat the greedy ladder.

On the other 22, family M's floor is width − 1 on 21 and width − 2 on one, every one a C refutation on a minor at about 30% of the vertices whose width the C re-proves exactly. So on 21 classes the pathwidth is width − 1 or width, and five floors rose above the record (from 2 or 3 up to 7, 8 and 9). Harper's ceiling is below the recorded width on all 24 (by 1 to 5), so the expansion family cannot close any of them under any computation. Family B gives 2 to 5 and sees only fringes. All 47 certificates verified.

